Ship the "offscreen" (and "minimal") Qt platform plugins in Slicer packages

Rationale: a headless Slicer (ModuleServer: no visible windows, streams its module GUIs) needs a QPA that
does not touch the display server. Every Qt build has `qoffscreen` and `qminimal`, but the packages only
install the native platform plugin (cocoa / xcb / windows). With the plugins shipped, `-platform offscreen`
works on all three platforms with the stock package (Qt 6 offscreen on macOS also provides an OpenGL
context; on Linux/Windows it does not -- fine for a ModuleServer, which renders nothing itself).
Cost: ~1 MB per package. No behavior change for normal launches.

--- a/CMake/SlicerCPack.cmake
+++ b/CMake/SlicerCPack.cmake
@@
     if(APPLE)
       list(APPEND SlicerBlockInstallQtPlugins_subdirectories
         platforms:cocoa
+        platforms:offscreen
+        platforms:minimal
         )
     elseif(UNIX)
       list(APPEND SlicerBlockInstallQtPlugins_subdirectories
         platforms:xcb
+        platforms:offscreen
+        platforms:minimal
         xcbglintegrations:xcb-glx-integration
         )
     elseif(WIN32)
       list(APPEND SlicerBlockInstallQtPlugins_subdirectories
         platforms:windows
+        platforms:offscreen
+        platforms:minimal
         )
     endif()
